Connect environmental and workplace evidence with process sources, transport, and ongoing work (@metal-environment-residuals: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @metals-and-metallurgical-production, #source "../sources/Nonferrous-Metals-Industries-BREF.lingua#r_19ZD7KKDWVWM20MXVNCQZJMCDB", #source "../sources/Iron-and-Steel-Production-BREF.lingua#r_1R9HC6SENF991ZZQA5WKH2C8HD", #source "../sources/Smitheries-and-Foundries-BREF.lingua#r_7ZJ5479WTSPDER11K364F6T041", #source "../sources/Rare-Earth-Production-Processing-and-Recycling-EPA.lingua#r_1GYVPYR8E6Q2CGEDBXQYDJYP9Q", #metals-and-metallurgical-production "Collection-sorting-recycling-metallurgy-and-quality-limits.lingua#r_5S3S2PXFEJMD6S0CEV434HSSNT") { r_0Z0Q9C4E51648GMA5TCX0J9X2R
**Read:** [Non-ferrous Metals Industries — European Commission BREF](../sources/Nonferrous-Metals-Industries-BREF.lingua#r_19ZD7KKDWVWM20MXVNCQZJMCDB), all complete relevant shared and metal-specific environmental/measurement chapters; [Iron and Steel Production — European Commission BREF](../sources/Iron-and-Steel-Production-BREF.lingua#r_1R9HC6SENF991ZZQA5WKH2C8HD), whole selected gas/water/residual and integrated process cases; [Smitheries and Foundries Industry — European Commission BREF](../sources/Smitheries-and-Foundries-BREF.lingua#r_7ZJ5479WTSPDER11K364F6T041), complete relevant foundry/process and control methods; [Rare Earth Elements: Production, Processing, Recycling, and Environmental Issues — U.S. EPA](../sources/Rare-Earth-Production-Processing-and-Recycling-EPA.lingua#r_1GYVPYR8E6Q2CGEDBXQYDJYP9Q), the entire environmental/production context for the chosen specialty case.

Metal production/fabrication creates interacting gas, dust, liquid, solid, thermal, noise, and other exposure/residual pathways. Chemical form, particle/support, concentration and mass flux, contact/time, location, and transformation matter. A bulk waste mass or a single concentration does not fully characterize either workplace exposure or long-term behavior.

Trace generation, transport, capture/treatment, recovered products, recycling, storage, and final pathways with conserved constituents and actual measured methods. A control device's nominal efficiency and a changed reported concentration can differ from real source or exposure reduction. Returns and treatment products can move or concentrate constituents elsewhere.

Compare technical alternatives through complete process, utilities, product quality, residuals, maintenance, affected people, and continuing work. Use actual current primary requirements and appropriate methods when a practical study depends on them; dated BREF examples and voluntary targets have their own scope and are not universal legal or exposure criteria.

**Work:** reconstruct a full public environmental/workplace or residual-system case with primary methods and quantitative boundaries. Independently balance a consequential constituent and test competing generation/transport/measurement explanations. Compare an alternative process/control arrangement and a changed operating state. Explain which observations would revise the conclusion and who must maintain, interpret, and respond after the nominal production task ends.

**Continue:** [Evaluate recycling through whole products, element pathways, and usable recovered material](Collection-sorting-recycling-metallurgy-and-quality-limits.lingua#r_5S3S2PXFEJMD6S0CEV434HSSNT).

**Return:** [Metals and metallurgical production — feed, refining, structure, useful products, and recovery](../Metals-and-metallurgical-production.lingua#r_59BDAQXT81552YF5F8TH4KQQH1).
